# =============================================================================
# DeepResearch Agent — Tool-layer environment variable configuration template
# =============================================================================
# Usage:
#   1. Copy the settings you need from this file into .env.local (gitignored, will not be committed)
#   2. Fill in real values
#   3. The program reads it automatically at startup; no source changes needed
#
# Design principles:
#   All API keys, URLs, and timeout parameters are read from .env; constructor arguments serve only as overrides.
#
# [Quick reference: availability from mainland China]
#   ✅ Directly accessible from mainland China (no VPN needed)
#   ⚠️  May be unstable in mainland China (VPN recommended)
#   ❌ Blocked in mainland China (VPN required)
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web Search tool configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend choice: serpapi | bing (default serpapi; both are accessible from mainland China)
#SEARCH_BACKEND=serpapi

# --- SerpAPI configuration (✅ accessible from mainland China, 100 free calls per month)---
# Register at https://serpapi.com to get a key
#SERPAPI_KEY=your_serpapi_key_here
#SERPAPI_ENDPOINT=https://serpapi.com/search

# --- Bing Search API configuration (✅ stable in mainland China, requires an Azure subscription)---
# Create a "Bing Search v7" resource in the Azure Portal to get a key
#BING_SEARCH_KEY=your_bing_key_here
#BING_SEARCH_ENDPOINT=https://api.bing.microsoft.com/v7.0/search

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ArXiv / paper reading tool configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend choice: semantic_scholar | arxiv (default semantic_scholar, accessible from mainland China)
# Why is semantic_scholar the default?
#   - semantic_scholar: ✅ reachable from mainland China, covers 200M+ papers, free
#   - arxiv:           ❌ blocked in mainland China, VPN required
#ARXIV_READER_BACKEND=semantic_scholar

# --- Semantic Scholar configuration (✅ reachable from mainland China, recommended)---
# Apply for a free key (optional; without a key there is a rate limit):
# https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form
#SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=your_ss_key_here

# --- ArXiv configuration (❌ blocked in mainland China unless you have a VPN)---
#ARXIV_API_ENDPOINT=http://export.arxiv.org/api/query

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser tool configuration (✅ plain HTTP fetching; availability in mainland China depends on the target site)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTTP request timeout (seconds)
#BROWSER_TIMEOUT=15

# Custom User-Agent (some websites require a specific UA)
#BROWSER_USER_AGENT=Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code Sandbox tool configuration (✅ purely local, no network)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default execution timeout (seconds)
#CODE_SANDBOX_TIMEOUT=10

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File Reader tool configuration (✅ purely local, no network)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sandbox root directory: only files under this directory may be read (strongly recommended in production)
#FILE_READER_ALLOWED_BASE_DIR=/path/to/allowed/data

# Maximum file size (bytes)
#FILE_READER_MAX_FILE_SIZE=10485760
